Subject: Cantor Succeeding SOP Proposal P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] b340afde-5437-4267-9344-06f81e47d880
@ [canonical_uuid] cb503c5b-bbf6-433b-b65f-31683d73a7ac

& [Decision]
  + implement the pure SWA-06A contract now because it advances the user-visible self-working sequence independently of the blocked B1 writer-host decision
  + select a ready lifecycle step rather than a globally complete plan because the succeeding-SOP proposal is itself one governed plan action
  + require every direct dependency complete so update verification and publication proposals can be causal prerequisites without hardcoding future SWA-05 receipt schemas
  + require exact derived work evidence so callers cannot omit causal evidence or inflate unrelated authority-looking references
  + preserve exact raw source bytes in memory because reformatting before review would break authorship and source lineage
  + produce a machine receipt but keep semantic review satisfaction signature activation and persistence separate

& [RejectedAlternatives]
  + do not infer B1 npm or desktop host selection
  + do not call a model or label a fixture as live self-authorship
  + do not reuse the full process-procedure authorship lane as authority because it adds unrelated runtime subjects
  + do not write directly into source_documents or specifications from the product module
  + do not accept opaque evidence supersets or caller-declared dependencies
  + do not combine authorship with self-signature or activation

& [ExpectedValue]
  + Cantor gains an executable provider-free boundary for proposing its next SOP from an exact causal work state
  + SWA-07 can later compose this output with boot work update and publication fixtures without redesigning authorship lineage
